{
  "name": "Emissary of the Great Accord",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC%20Button%20Icons/BBTTCC_button_icon_peace_1.png",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>Emissary of the Great Accord.</strong> You are no longer just a person with opinions. You are a walking offer of peace with teeth.</p><ul><li><p>Once per Soma Break, when a scene involving multiple factions or hostile forces reaches its tipping point, you can invoke this feature as an action.</p></li><li><p>Declare what peace or unity would look like here. All creatures and factions involved that can see or hear you must make a Soul check against your Harmony Marshal save DC (your Resolve DC).</p></li><li><p>On a failure, they are compelled for 1 minute to treat you as a legitimate mediator and to consider your proposed outcome as a serious option. They can defend themselves if directly attacked, but are disinclined to escalate.</p></li><li><p>At the GM’s discretion, if this scene is resolved through this power toward genuine reconciliation, you may trigger a larger-world effect such as <strong>Loyalty +1</strong> and/or <strong>Unity +1</strong> in the relevant region, and <strong>Darkness –1</strong> if the outcome meaningfully heals something broken.</p></li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
